  "description": "*“Ba-woo, will you be my mate?”*\n\nDeep within the remote mountains—with the peaks and fields as his only companions—lived Ba-woo: an earnest young woodcutter of striking beauty who spent his days brewing makgeolli and tending to his crops.\nHe had prayed and pleaded endlessly to the Mountain Spirit to grant him a worthy mate,\nbut the only thing that ever answered his prayers was the trail of hoofprints left by a thieving roe deer that had raided his precious fields!\n\nThen one day, slumped beside a shattered makgeolli jar, Ba-woo discovered an unconscious, naked man—a figure with dark skin, rippling muscles, and a pair of jutting fangs that were strangely alluring.\n\nIn that very instant, he realized the truth:  \nAt long last, the Mountain Spirit had sent him a mate!\n\n*“Come on, let’s hurry home and mate!”*  \n\n*“M-mate?! I mean... isn't it a bit too soon for us to be mating?”*  \n\n*“Or would you rather do it right here? I’m certainly up for it.”*\n\n***Note: The description used on LezhinUS is currently incorrect. It is the description meant for The Ghost in the Doorway**",
